.idea/*

# ---- guild v5 board (plugins/guild) ------------------------------------------------
#
# The board is a Turso database, and the database is DERIVED state: `guild rebuild`
# replays .guild/journal.ndjson into it. So git carries config.yaml, journal.ndjson and
# export/ — and MUST carry them. A blanket `.guild/` ignore (which is what this file
# used to have) means the journal is never committed, and then the first person to run
# `guild journal compact` on a fresh clone snapshots an empty database over the only
# record of the project's history.
#
# Derived, machine-local, or a repair artifact — never commit these:
.guild/guild.db
.guild/guild.db-*
.guild/guild.db.*
.guild/spool/
.guild/*.tmp.*
.guild/.export.tmp.*/
.guild/journal.pending
.guild/dashboard.html
.guild/backup-*/

# The v4 board that predates the v5 rewrite. Left untracked deliberately: `guild init`
# MOVES it to .guild/v4-archive/ rather than importing it (design §11), and this
# repository is the plugin's own source, not a project whose board history matters.
.guild/requirements/
.guild/tasks/
.guild/plans/
.guild/reviews/
.guild/archive/
.guild/v4-archive*/
.guild/docs/
.guild/qa/
.guild/state.yaml
.guild/BOARD.md

# Python bytecode from local script runs
__pycache__/
*.pyc
